  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001 Just Energy Transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal: Develop a programme on Just Energy Transition (JET) build on needs and positioning from the Global South in the light of the urgency of the climate crisis.
Why strategic: The transition from a high carbon to a low/ zero carbon economy is underway.The risk is real that this (energy) transition will increase inequalities, poverty, and food insecurity, especially in low-income countries. As risks become realities, we expect donors to become more interested in achieving a Just Energy Transition. Suchaprogramme (on a just energy transition) would align well with Oxfams DNA and is Oxfam&apos;s USP as it brings together the climate and the inequality agendas.
Making most of existing opportunities: Different initiatives (within ONL, Oxfam and beyond) are happening to explore different views and perspectives on JET (e.g. AACJ, Fair4All, FFG, OCI, Oxfam JET taskforce). The opportunity is to break the silos between all these initiatives and to start working more towards an integrated vision, making this the basis of a new programme on JET.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
